In the literature the site is denoted $\text{Lis-ét}(\mathcal{X})$ or $\text{Lis-Et}(\mathcal{X})$ and the associated topos is denoted $\mathcal{X}_{\text{lis-é}t}$ or $\mathcal{X}_{\text{lis-et}}$. In the Stacks project our convention is to name the site and denote the corresponding topos by $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$.